[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/UI/Pulp/PulpPortraitRoundel.cs" id="3_frame"]
; Fighter VS variant (TG-SCREENS, UI_SPEC_GLASS 9.2): the bg0 field and the screen streak; two 320 px portrait frames
; (P1 left at x 280, P2 right at x 1320, y 300) with a 2 px edge and a 14 px glow in the slot colour; the hero names in
; T40 under them, each with its player label and slot shape; "VS" in T01 with the title gradient centred at y 420;
; the stage name in T14 under it and the stage preview on a small glass slab, the three stacked in one centred column
; (Middle, its top at y 345) so a larger UI scale pushes them down together instead of overlapping. PlayerPortrait / OpponentPortrait,
; PlayerName / OpponentName, StageNameLabel and StagePreview are filled by LoadingScreen.Configure from the live
; SessionData; each hides itself when its source is unset. The frame edges and glows, the slot shapes, the gradient
; and the streak are added in code.

